## Context

Child of master ticket 0650. `check_two_processes_both_answer` currently grades
only that three query calls return hit lists without raising. It records result
identity but does not require it, and a real seeded run passed with three empty
lists. This child owns that acceptance arm only; failover accounting is 0652
and the full soak is 0653.

## Actions

- Establish a non-empty expected item-key projection before company arrives;
  report `not-run` when the target cannot establish that premise.
- Require both concurrently live processes and the post-pair process to preserve
  that projection. Empty, missing or divergent projections are failures.
- Record only privacy-safe projections and comparison facts, not full replies.
- Add focused readable-corruption controls alongside the existing unreadable
  post-pair control.

## Test

- [ ] Quiet shared-root fixture passes with a known hit.
- [ ] Empty, changed, live-divergent and post-pair-divergent controls each fail.
- [ ] Different roots and an unprovable baseline report `not-run`.
- [ ] Each fail-control is red only on its intended check.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The assertion cannot pass merely because a query returned.
- [ ] Targeted unit tests and acceptance fixtures pass.
- [ ] Real-target evidence is committed or its unavailable premise is reported
      as a non-pass state.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
